title: Analytics › Program filter
route: /analytics
intro: The 'All programs' menu narrows every figure, chart and breakdown to one level of care: Residential, IOP, PHP or Withdrawal management. The demo has no per-program split of its decisions, so a small weighting table does it, the same way every time.
dir: TD
also: Demo values. The weights are invented: shares of decisions 40 / 30 / 20 / 10, and a shift in approval, turnaround, advice and edits for each program. They are balanced so 'All programs' stays the starting set (71%, 29%, 2.4 days, 207). The labels follow the sidebar's words 'Residential' and 'Withdrawal management'; the Dashboard's Program filter says 'Residential 3.5' and 'Detox'.
---
start s1 "Click the 'All programs' menu"
overlay o1 "'All programs', 'Residential', 'IOP', 'PHP', 'Withdrawal management'"
input i1 "Pick a program\nOr press Arrow keys, Enter; Esc closes"
process p1 "The pill turns green-edged and bold\n'Clear filters' appears beside the menus"

group gScale "What the weights do"
  process w1 "Volume: the program's share of decisions\nResidential 40%, IOP 30%, PHP 20%, Withdrawal management 10%\nApplies to decisions, drafts, requests helped, rulings and accepted denials"
  process w2 "Approval: every payer's rate moves by a few points\nResidential -3, IOP +4, PHP +2, Withdrawal management -4\nThe denials follow: decisions times the rest"
  process w3 "Turnaround: payer averages times a multiplier\nResidential 1.10, IOP 0.95, PHP 0.95, Withdrawal management 0.85"
  process w4 "Reasons: each payer's denials are spread over its reasons\nFixable reasons weigh more in IOP and PHP, less in Residential and Withdrawal management\nSo the preventable share moves: about 62% in Residential, 71% in IOP"
  process w5 "Advice taken works and the draft edits shift a few points the same way"
endgroup

process r1 "Every number on the page is added up again from the same table\nTiles, bars, preventable rows, denial table, 'What helps most', report and files"
process r2 "Recorded events join only if their request is in that program\nAppeal rulings, accepted denials, dismissed recommendations\nThe request is looked up on the Dashboard or in Authorizations"
process r3 "Workload counts the Dashboard's requests in that program\nIt does not follow the period"
decision q1 "20 or more decisions (or denials) left?"
screen ok "Numbers show"
screen hid "'-' and 'Not enough decisions yet'\nMore likely with one payer and a small program, for example Lakeshore and Withdrawal management"
click cl "Click 'Clear filters' or pick 'All programs'"
process p2 "Program and payer back to all\nThe starting figures return exactly"
goto g1 "Continues in: Analytics › Monthly report › What the files contain"
end e1 "Page matches the program"

s1 --> o1 --> i1 --> p1
i1 --> w1 & w2 & w3 & w4 & w5
w1 & w2 & w3 & w4 & w5 --> r1
r1 --> q1
q1 -->|Yes| ok --> e1
q1 -->|No| hid --> e1
r1 -.-> r2
r1 -.-> r3
p1 --> cl --> p2
r1 -.-> g1
